 "note": "The register of function identifiers. Read, never recomputed. An identifier is given once and never changes, so a name that is already here keeps its number no matter where it moves in the code. Frozen 2026-08-26 from the 455 assignments the positional scheme had produced, before the sweep was widened. RETIRED numbers are kept with the reason: a number is given once and never handed to anything else, even when it was issued by mistake and referenced nowhere.",
 "renamed": {
  "spending": "expenses",
  "theCushion": "theEmergencyFund"
 },
 "retired": {
  "MK-CF-F-047": "a pure alias of effectiveRateOnGross, itself part of a second tax function. Deleted 2026-08-27 when the two functions were collapsed into one. Retired, never reused.",
  "MK-CF-F-093": "one of five functions forming a SECOND, single-filer-only tax function that ran beside the filing-status-aware one. Superseded by MK-CF-F-097 taxableIncomeFor on 2026-08-27. Retired, never reused.",
  "MK-CF-F-094": "same second function \u2014 superseded by marginalBracketFor. It reached the Roth-vs-Traditional lean, which read a single-filer bracket for everyone. Retired, never reused.",
  "MK-CF-F-095": "same second function \u2014 superseded by taxOwedFor. Retired, never reused.",
  "MK-CF-F-096": "same second function \u2014 superseded by effectiveRateOnGrossFor. Retired, never reused.",
  "MK-CF-F-123": "stamped a date from the local clock in the cash-flow code while two screens declared their own `iso` using toISOString (UTC), so an evening entry west of UTC was filed in the next month. Renamed isoLocalDate on 2026-08-27 so the name says why. Retired, never reused.",
  "MK-CF-F-147": "issued 2026-08-27 to basePay as a plain function. basePay is an ORCHESTRATOR, and the founder ruled the same day that orchestrators carry type O so they are identifiable at a glance. Re-issued on the O counter. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-CF-F-154": "issued 2026-08-27 to spending as a plain function. spending is an ORCHESTRATOR, and the founder ruled the same day that orchestrators carry type O so they are identifiable at a glance. Re-issued on the O counter. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-CF-F-158": "issued 2026-08-27 to thisMonth as a plain function. thisMonth is an ORCHESTRATOR, and the founder ruled the same day that orchestrators carry type O so they are identifiable at a glance. Re-issued on the O counter. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-CF-O-009": "issued to expenses before the rename from spending was recorded; spending already held MK-CF-O-002",
  "MK-NW-F-074": "issued to theEmergencyFund on 2026-09-28 only because its ORCHESTRATOR marker had been written as /* \u2026 */, which write-headers.py owns and overwrote. It is an orchestrator; it carries MK-NW-O-004 across from theCushion, the name it was renamed from.",
  "MK-NW-F-102": "rateWhereItRefuses \u2014 the money-weighted rate per year that stood in where the window return refused (Q52, mock v17 mark 16). Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted, and nothing stands in for one. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-NW-O-009": "issued 2026-10-04 to whyNoReturn by mistake \u2014 it was written directly under the orchestrator marker that belongs to thePerformance, so it was typed as an orchestrator. It is a dependent function and is re-issued in F. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-PF-F-024": "userFlows \u2014 a helper of the money-weighted rate (moneyWeighted.ts). Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-PF-F-025": "historyIsComplete \u2014 a helper of the money-weighted rate (moneyWeighted.ts). Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-PF-F-026": "moneyWeightedReturn \u2014 the money-weighted rate per year (XIRR). Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-PF-F-027": "isMoneyWeighted \u2014 a helper of the money-weighted rate (moneyWeighted.ts). Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-PF-F-030": "npv \u2014 a helper of the money-weighted rate (moneyWeighted.ts). Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-PL-F-076": "the name \"num\" meant two different contracts \u2014 one returned 0 when a value could not be read, the other returned NaN. Split into numOrZero and numOrNaN on 2026-08-27, each with its own number. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-ST-F-064": "modifiedDietzOverWindow \u2014 the Modified Dietz return over a window. Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-XS-F-010": "investableChangePct \u2014 the change in balance on cash + investments. Removed 2026-10-04 by the owner decision DEC-1669: every return is time-weighted. This number is never reused.",
  "MK-XS-F-117": "the name \"daysBetween\" meant three different contracts \u2014 clamped-at-zero, signed, and absolute-fractional. Split into daysSince, daysBetweenDates and daysApart on 2026-08-27, each with its own number. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-XS-F-150": "issued 2026-08-27 to a MoneyKeel/functions/cashflow function in family XS by mistake \u2014 that folder was not in the family map, so it fell to the default. Re-issued in CF as MK-CF-F-140. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-XS-F-151": "issued 2026-08-27 to a MoneyKeel/functions/cashflow function in family XS by mistake \u2014 that folder was not in the family map, so it fell to the default. Re-issued in CF as MK-CF-F-141. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-XS-F-152": "issued 2026-08-27 to a MoneyKeel/functions/cashflow function in family XS by mistake \u2014 that folder was not in the family map, so it fell to the default. Re-issued in CF as MK-CF-F-142. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
  "MK-XS-F-153": "issued 2026-08-27 to a MoneyKeel/functions/cashflow function in family XS by mistake \u2014 that folder was not in the family map, so it fell to the default. Re-issued in CF as MK-CF-F-143. This number is retired and is never handed to anything else.",
